<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kgalema Motlanthe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1949–</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kgalema Motlanthe is a South African politician who was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> from September 2008 to May 2009, after the ANC recalled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thabo-mbeki">Thabo Mbeki</a>. A former trade unionist and ANC secretary-general, he served as a caretaker until the 2009 election and was then deputy president under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacob-zuma">Jacob Zuma</a> until 2014.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kgalema-motlanthe.jpg" alt="Kgalema Motlanthe" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Copyright Economic Forum (www.weforum.org) / Eric Miller emiller@iafrica.com · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kgalema_Motlanthe,_2009_World_Economic_Forum_on_Africa-1_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
